WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.630
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Writing Skills.

2
00:00:04.930 --> 00:00:08.201
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.501 --> 00:00:14.915
Unit seventeen: CV and Cover Letter. Today you will write a short CV and a cover letter.

4
00:00:15.215 --> 00:00:17.902
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:18.867 --> 00:00:21.937
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:22.783 --> 00:00:23.692
CV.

7
00:00:24.683 --> 00:00:27.588
CV means a document about your education and work.

8
00:00:28.183 --> 00:00:29.568
Update your CV.

9
00:00:30.183 --> 00:00:32.476
Your turn. Say: CV.

10
00:00:35.333 --> 00:00:36.346
CV.

11
00:00:37.083 --> 00:00:38.189
Experience.

12
00:00:39.183 --> 00:00:42.448
Experience means work or skills from the past.

13
00:00:43.050 --> 00:00:45.108
I have two years of experience.

14
00:00:45.717 --> 00:00:48.485
Your turn. Say: Experience.

15
00:00:51.333 --> 00:00:52.671
Experience.

16
00:00:53.417 --> 00:00:54.244
Skill.

17
00:00:55.250 --> 00:00:57.702
Skill means an ability to do something well.

18
00:00:58.317 --> 00:01:00.107
Computer skills are useful.

19
00:01:00.717 --> 00:01:03.299
Your turn. Say: Skill.

20
00:01:06.133 --> 00:01:07.042
Skill.

21
00:01:07.783 --> 00:01:08.970
Qualification.

22
00:01:09.983 --> 00:01:12.772
Qualification means a certificate or degree.

23
00:01:13.383 --> 00:01:15.453
She has a teaching qualification.

24
00:01:16.050 --> 00:01:19.144
Your turn. Say: Qualification.

25
00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:23.245
Qualification.

26
00:01:23.983 --> 00:01:24.938
Reference.

27
00:01:25.950 --> 00:01:28.948
Reference means a person who can say good things about you.

28
00:01:29.550 --> 00:01:31.004
Give two references.

29
00:01:31.617 --> 00:01:34.025
Your turn. Say: Reference.

30
00:01:36.867 --> 00:01:37.926
Reference.

31
00:01:38.683 --> 00:01:39.510
Position.

32
00:01:40.517 --> 00:01:42.110
Position means a job.

33
00:01:42.717 --> 00:01:44.542
I am applying for the position.

34
00:01:45.150 --> 00:01:47.535
Your turn. Say: Position.

35
00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:51.308
Position.

36
00:01:52.050 --> 00:01:53.016
Achieve.

37
00:01:54.017 --> 00:01:56.701
Achieve means to succeed in doing something.

38
00:01:57.317 --> 00:01:59.038
I achieved good results.

39
00:01:59.650 --> 00:02:02.685
Your turn. Say: Achieve.

40
00:02:05.533 --> 00:02:06.569
Achieve.

41
00:02:07.317 --> 00:02:08.771
Enthusiastic.

42
00:02:09.783 --> 00:02:13.118
Enthusiastic means very interested and excited.

43
00:02:13.717 --> 00:02:15.856
I am enthusiastic about teaching.

44
00:02:16.450 --> 00:02:19.671
Your turn. Say: Enthusiastic.

45
00:02:22.533 --> 00:02:23.801
Enthusiastic.

46
00:02:24.600 --> 00:02:28.309
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:29.150 --> 00:02:31.289
Visal, what goes in a CV?

48
00:02:32.383 --> 00:02:42.780
Put your contact details, education, work experience, skills and references. Keep it to one or two pages and use clear headings.

49
00:02:43.883 --> 00:02:45.337
What about a cover letter?

50
00:02:46.450 --> 00:02:54.048
It explains why you want the job and why you are suitable. Start with the position you are applying for.

51
00:02:55.150 --> 00:02:57.045
How do I describe my past work?

52
00:02:58.150 --> 00:03:07.896
Use action verbs in the past tense, such as managed, taught and organised. For example, I organised a team of ten students.

53
00:03:09.033 --> 00:03:10.557
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:11.417 --> 00:03:13.973
Grammar focus: Action verbs.

55
00:03:14.273 --> 00:03:15.530
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:16.217 --> 00:03:18.506
I organised a team of ten students.

57
00:03:19.417 --> 00:03:21.056
I taught English to beginners.

58
00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:28.507
Use strong action verbs in the past tense to describe your experience. Keep sentences short and specific.

59
00:03:29.250 --> 00:03:33.168
Be careful! Don't say: I organise a team last year.

60
00:03:35.133 --> 00:03:38.166
Say: I organised a team last year.

61
00:03:38.466 --> 00:03:39.781
Use past tense.

62
00:03:40.567 --> 00:03:43.091
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:43.900 --> 00:03:45.319
Applying for a Job.

64
00:03:45.619 --> 00:03:48.431
Rotha applies for a job as a teaching assistant.

65
00:03:49.433 --> 00:03:52.327
His CV lists his education and two skills.

66
00:03:53.333 --> 00:03:56.088
He uses action verbs like taught and organised.

67
00:03:57.100 --> 00:04:00.237
His cover letter says he is enthusiastic about teaching.

68
00:04:01.233 --> 00:04:03.779
He includes two references at the end.

69
00:04:04.867 --> 00:04:08.868
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:09.717 --> 00:04:12.181
A CV lists your education and blank.

71
00:04:12.481 --> 00:04:16.215
A, food. B, pets. C, experience.

72
00:04:19.767 --> 00:04:21.929
The answer is C: experience.

73
00:04:23.083 --> 00:04:25.489
A cover letter explains why you are blank.

74
00:04:25.789 --> 00:04:29.036
A, suitable. B, tired. C, late.

75
00:04:32.600 --> 00:04:34.414
The answer is A: suitable.

76
00:04:35.550 --> 00:04:37.909
Action verbs describe past blank.

77
00:04:38.209 --> 00:04:41.259
A, food. B, work. C, weather.

78
00:04:44.800 --> 00:04:46.625
The answer is B: work.

79
00:04:47.783 --> 00:04:49.992
Enthusiastic means very blank.

80
00:04:50.292 --> 00:04:54.607
A, sleepy. B, angry. C, excited.

81
00:04:58.167 --> 00:05:00.236
The answer is C: excited.

82
00:05:01.383 --> 00:05:03.952
Rotha applies for a job as a teaching blank.

83
00:05:04.252 --> 00:05:07.998
A, assistant. B, pilot. C, farmer.

84
00:05:11.533 --> 00:05:13.765
The answer is A: assistant.

85
00:05:14.967 --> 00:05:18.141
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:18.983 --> 00:05:20.542
How do you write a CV?

87
00:05:29.350 --> 00:05:30.932
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:31.232 --> 00:05:44.405
I list my contact details, education, work experience and skills with clear headings. I use action verbs in the past tense. I keep the CV short and write a cover letter for the position.

89
00:05:44.705 --> 00:05:46.554
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:47.450 --> 00:05:51.252
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and action verbs.

91
00:05:51.552 --> 00:05:56.990
Today's value is professionalism. Be prepared, polite and reliable in everything you do.

92
00:05:57.290 --> 00:05:59.885
See you in Unit eighteen. Goodbye!

93
00:06:00.185 --> 00:06:03.000
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

